parse(String) -- parse XML
**************************

  * Function: *note parse: parse_lpString_rp,
  * Usage: 
        parse s
  * Inputs:
      * s, a *note string: (Macaulay2Doc)String,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Trim => ..., default value true
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note XMLnode: XMLnode,, a tree of hash tables
        resulting from parsing the contents of s as XML

Description
===========

This function parses XML into a tree of hash tables of type *note XMLnode:
XMLnode,.

+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : x = parse ///<foo a="hi there">ho there<bar/></foo>///  |
|                                                             |
|o1 = <foo a="hi there"                                       |
|       "ho there"                                            |
|       <bar                                                  |
|                                                             |
|o1 : XMLnode                                                 |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : peek'_3 x                                               |
|                                                             |
|o2 = XMLnode{"a" => "hi there"                              }|
|             children => {"ho there", XMLnode{tag => "bar"}} |
|             tag => "foo"                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : x#"a"                                                   |
|                                                             |
|o3 = hi there                                                |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : x.children                                              |
|                                                             |
|o4 = {ho there, <bar}                                        |
|                                                             |
|o4 : List                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : class \ oo                                              |
|                                                             |
|o5 = {String, XMLnode}                                       |
|                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                    |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : x.tag                                                   |
|                                                             |
|o6 = foo                                                     |
+-------------------------------------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note parse(String): parse_lpString_rp, -- parse XML
